@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title Activity - generativeaiagent/DataSource
skinparam activity {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  diamondBackgroundColor #e2e8f0
  diamondBorderColor #1d4ed8
  diamondFontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
  barColor #1d4ed8
}
start
partition "Observe and Bind" {
:Start from shared flow\nshared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg;
:Read desired DataSource spec, tracked status,\nand delete intent;
if ("Tracked or explicit OCI identity present?") then (yes)
:Get the current OCI resource via GetDataSource;
else (no)
:Resolve an existing OCI resource through\nListDataSources using filters compartmentId,\nknowledgeBaseId, displayName;
:Create the OCI resource via CreateDataSource\nwhen no reusable match is found;
:Persist the resolved or created OCI identity\ninto status;
endif
}
if ("Delete requested?") then (yes)
partition "Delete" {
:Delete path uses DeleteDataSource with\nrequired via GetDataSource or ListDataSources\nto DELETED confirmation;
:Confirm deletion via GetDataSource or\nListDataSources until OCI reaches DELETED;
if ("Delete cleanup and finalizer release succeed?") then (yes)
:Remove the finalizer after delete completion;
else (no)
:Stay blocked until cleanup or finalizer\nrelease succeeds;
endif
}
stop
else (no)
partition "Lifecycle Classification" {
if ("OCI state in retryable set?") then (yes)
:Request requeue while OCI remains in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING;
stop
endif
if ("OCI state is outside success targets?") then (yes)
:Return an unsuccessful reconcile result until\nOCI reaches ACTIVE, INACTIVE;
stop
endif
}
partition "Ready and Drift Handling" {
:Compare live OCI state against the\nrepo-authored mutation surface;
if ("Force-new or conflicting drift detected?") then (yes)
:Reject drift before OCI mutation for force-new\nfields compartmentId, knowledgeBaseId;
stop
endif
if ("Supported mutable drift detected?") then (yes)
:Apply UpdateDataSource only for mutable fields\ndataSourceConfig, definedTags, description,\ndisplayName (+2 more);
else (no)
:Skip the no-op mutation path;
endif
:Run provider helper hooks\ncreate=tfresource.CreateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForWorkRequestWithErrorHandling\nentity=datasource action=CREATED;\nupdate=tfresource.UpdateResource,\ntfresource.WaitForWorkRequestWithErrorHandling\nentity=datasource action=UPDATED;\ndelete=tfresource.DeleteResource,\ntfresource.WaitForWorkRequestWithErrorHandling\nentity=datasource action=DELETED when the\nmatching field-driven path executes;
:Apply explicit follow-up semantics\ncreate=GetWorkRequest -> GetDataSource;\nupdate=GetWorkRequest -> GetDataSource;\ndelete=GetWorkRequest ->\nGetDataSource/ListDataSources confirm-delete;
:Return success for the ACTIVE, INACTIVE\nsuccess state;
:Project required status and finalizer policy\nretain-until-confirmed-delete;
:Requeue on provisioning, updating, terminating;
}
endif
stop
note right
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg
Start from the shared reconcile activity and
specialize provider-backed CRUD, wait, and
status-projection details here.
Controller-local activity diagrams add
list-lookup hints, secret policies, delete
handling, and open formal gaps.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers specialize the shared reconcile path
with formal runtime ownership.
service: generativeaiagent
slug: datasource
kind: DataSource
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update
UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource; update=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource; delete=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource/ListDataSources confirm-delete
supported drift: dataSourceConfig, definedTags,
description, displayName (+2 more)
reject before mutate: force-new fields
compartmentId, knowledgeBaseId
create-only fields: none
list lookup:
oci_generative_ai_agent_data_sources filters
compartmentId, knowledgeBaseId, displayName;
exact compartmentId plus knowledgeBaseId plus
displayName unique match in ACTIVE, INACTIVE,
CREATING, or UPDATING; duplicate matches fail
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
Reviewed lifecycle mapping treats CREATING as
provisioning, UPDATING as updating, ACTIVE and
INACTIVE as success, and DELETING as
terminating; FAILED is terminal and DELETED is
only a delete-confirmation target.
CreateDataSource returns a DataSource body plus
opc-work-request-id, while UpdateDataSource and
DeleteDataSource return work-request headers
without a resource body. The runtime prefers the
create response identifier and otherwise
recovers the DataSource OCID from work-request
resources before rereading GetDataSource.
Pre-create reuse only runs when spec.displayName
is present and keeps exact compartmentId plus
knowledgeBaseId plus displayName matching
bounded to ACTIVE, INACTIVE, CREATING, or
UPDATING summaries.
Only displayName, description, dataSourceConfig,
metadata, freeformTags, and definedTags
reconcile in place; compartmentId and
knowledgeBaseId remain replacement-only.
Delete keeps the finalizer until the work
request is terminal and GetDataSource or
fallback ListDataSources confirms the resource
is gone.
Shared manifest promotion for this row is
intentionally deferred to the convergence story.
end note
@enduml
